692 0 obj
<<
/Title (Algorithms \(DSA\) project. It allows users to view available buses, search buses by destination, book tickets, cancel tickets, sort buses by fare and view the waiting queue. The project uses an ArrayList to maintain bus and booking records, a Queue to manage passengers waiting for a full bus, searching to locate buses and tickets, and sorting to arrange buses by fare. File handling is used to load bus information from buses.txt when the program starts and save updated seat availability when the user exits.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 559 0 R
/Prev 622 0 R
/Next 693 0 R
>>
endobj
693 0 obj
<<
/Title (The sample data contains two buses: B101 from Raipur to Bhopal with a fare of Rs. 700 and two seats, and B102 from Raipur to Nagpur with a fare of Rs. 450 and two seats. The first generated ticket ID is TKT101. The project demonstrates how basic DSA concepts can be combined to solve a practical reservation problem through a simple menu-driven interface.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 559 0 R
/Prev 692 0 R
/Next 623 0 R
>>
endobj
